the decision, restated for implementation
-------------------------------------------

ONE ACTIVATION LAYER over TWO IMPLEMENTATION SUBSTRATES. builtins
keep their scala table (descriptions, json schemas, annotations,
dispatch — the substrate); their NAMES additionally live in the ML
MCP_Tool registry so activation is uniform:

  declare [[mcp_tools del: repl_fork repl_merge repl_rebase]]
  bundle exploration = [[mcp_tools add: list_theories find_theorems]]

three pinned guardrails (spec, same section):

- AVAILABILITY FLOOR: empty builtins section in the MCP.tools
  payload (context without MCP_Tools import, no ML session, broken
  -T theory) -> scala serves the FULL builtin table. the old
  two-table merge is the degraded mode.
- ASYMMETRIC CALLABILITY: del'd builtin = unlisted but callable
  (tools/call dispatches builtin names scala-side BEFORE consulting
  activation — the existing dispatch order, kept deliberately);
  del'd ML tool = unlisted and uncallable (unchanged,
  MCP_Protocol.run_tool). no privileged non-scopable meta-core —
  unlisted-but-callable already makes lockout impossible.
- DRIFT GATE: mirror name set == builtin table name set, both
  directions, pinned over the live bridge.

data model delta (MCP_Tools.thy)
---------------------------------

- MCP_Tool.form grows a constructor: Builtin (form_tag "builtin").
- mirror declarations at the end of MCP_Tools.thy, one per scala
  builtin: MCP_Tool.declare with the one-line description duplicated
  from the scala table and run = (fn _ => fn _ => error "builtin
  tool: dispatched Isabelle/Scala-side"). registered active, like
  any top-level declaration. print_mcp_tools shows them as
  [builtin] rows for free.
- tools_body (MCP_Protocol) grows a second section: builtins =
  (name, active) for EVERY registered Builtin-form row — inactive
  rows included, so scala can tell "hidden" from "absent". Builtin
  rows are EXCLUDED from the existing ML-tool row list (they carry
  no real params/run and must not enter exposure-name computation).

scala delta (mcp_server.scala / mcp_session.scala)
---------------------------------------------------

- decode the builtins section alongside the tool rows.
- tools/list merge: builtin table rows filtered to active mirrors;
  empty section -> full table (the floor). still a pure function of
  (builtin table, decoded payload) — Fake_Backend testable.
- tools/call: UNCHANGED (builtin dispatch precedes activation; ML
  dispatch path already refuses inactive tools engine-side).

name/argument mapping across the layers
----------------------------------------

  mcp            tools/list only changes (which builtin rows appear)
  bridge         MCP.tools payload: (ml_rows, builtin_activation)
  engine (ml)    MCP_Tool registry: Builtin-form rows, active set

