ASSUMPTIONS -> tests
---------------------

- A1 mirror rows behave as ordinary registry entries: del/add round
  trip, visibility follows imports, run slot errors with the
  builtin message [ml unit, MCP-Tools-Tests].
- A2 the builtins section distinguishes hidden from absent: all
  mirrors del'd -> section full of (name, false) -> zero builtins
  listed; context without MCP_Tools -> empty section -> full table
  [scala unit: both payload shapes against Fake_Backend].
- A3 no exposure regression: a user ML tool named like a builtin
  still gets theory-qualified; the builtin keeps the bare name;
  Builtin rows never reach the exposure function [scala unit,
  existing collision tests extended].
- A4 drift gate: mirror set == table set both ways over the live
  bridge — fails when a builtin is added scala-side without a
  mirror, or a mirror outlives a removed builtin [bridge]. The gate
  reads MCP_Server.all_builtin_names, which sources the tool_scope
  trio from a hand-maintained literal (tool_scope_builtin_names) since
  those three close over per-connection state and cannot be listed
  statically; a scala-unit test welds that literal to what a fresh
  Handler actually serves, so a new connection-state tool added
  without updating both the literal and the mirror still fails a test
  rather than silently escaping the bridge gate [scala unit].
- A5 asymmetric callability: del'd builtin callable, del'd ML tool
  refused (uncallable) [bridge + e2e]. NOTE: the ML tool half is
  refused as "Undefined mcp tool" via the exposed-name path (an
  inactive row drops out of MCP_Tool.active entirely, so tools/call's
  name resolution never finds it), not "Inactive MCP tool" — that
  message is MCP_Protocol.run_tool's own, reachable only by dispatch
  on the internal name directly, which the ml-unit suite covers
  separately.
- A6 tool_scope interaction (plans/tool_scope landed first): a del in
  a repl-local context affects only designations reading that
  context; switching designation (tool_scope_set) switches the
  builtin listing accordingly, without touching the shared MCP_Tools
  theory other connections/tests read [bridge + e2e: "a del'd builtin
  mirror is unlisted but stays callable"].
